Error [E0068]: This callable puts the return type before the arrow.
  --> tests/ui/derive_generated_collision.jet:2:27
    |
  2 |     fn debug_string(self) String -> T.$name
    |                           ^^^^^^
 Why: A return type follows the one arrow: `fn name(...) -> Type { … }`. An effect ceiling splits that arrow: `fn name(...) -[Effects]> Type { … }`.
 Fix: Write `fn name(...) -> Type { … }`, or `fn name(...) -[Effects]> Type { … }`.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0068

Error [E0065]: This function uses the retired `::` body marker.
  --> tests/ui/derive_generated_collision.jet:10:39
    |
 10 | fn Point.debug_string(self) -> String :: "existing"
    |                                       ^^
 Why: Named function bodies use braces. `::` binds a name, and `=` fills a slot inside a definition.
 Fix: Replace `::` with `{ … }`; `jet fmt` applies this fix.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0065

Error [E0105]: Generated method `debug_string` from `derive T.DebugText` collides with existing method `Point.debug_string`
  --> tests/ui/derive_generated_collision.jet:2:8
    |
  2 |     fn debug_string(self) String -> T.$name
    |        ^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: `derive T.DebugText` and existing method `Point.debug_string` both define a member named `debug_string` on `Point`
 Fix: Rename the generated member in `derive T.DebugText`, or rename the colliding member
